photorec
Usage: photorec IMAGE_or_DEVICE

Carves files back off a formatted or damaged filesystem by their signatures --
it ignores the directory structure entirely and recognises file types from
their content, so it recovers data even when the filesystem is gone. Interactive.

	photorec image.img    carve from a ddrescue image (preferred)
	photorec /dev/sdX     carve from the device directly

Recovers file contents, not names -- expect `f0001234.jpg` style output.

See also: testdisk, ddrescue, file
